From: mementum-lcd
Subject: thorvg: include <string.h> where memcpy and memset are used

tvgRender.h uses memcpy and includes no string header at all; tvgCompressor.cpp
uses both and includes <memory.h>, which is not standard and does not reliably
declare them. Most toolchains pull them in transitively and nobody notices --
the ESP-IDF build of the same sources is fine. The ESP32 Arduino core's
toolchain does not, and the build stops with:

    tvgCompressor.cpp:116: error: 'memset' was not declared in this scope
    tvgRender.h:129:       error: 'memcpy' was not declared in this scope

Two includes. Worth sending upstream to ThorVG rather than carrying.

Applied by fetch-lvgl.sh.
---
--- a/src/libs/thorvg/tvgCompressor.cpp
+++ b/src/libs/thorvg/tvgCompressor.cpp
@@ -61,6 +61,7 @@
 
 #include <string>
 #include <memory.h>
+#include <string.h>
 #include "tvgCompressor.h"
 
 namespace tvg {
--- a/src/libs/thorvg/tvgRender.h
+++ b/src/libs/thorvg/tvgRender.h
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #define _TVG_RENDER_H_
 
 #include <math.h>
+#include <string.h>
 #include <cstdarg>
 #include "tvgCommon.h"
 #include "tvgArray.h"
